      "extract": "As we have seen in the last section, the shape of a hyperbolic ideal tetrahedron is completely determined by its dihedral angles. The notion of an angle structure is that these dihedral angles should ﬁt together coherently. Definition 3.1. An angle structure on an ideal triangulation τ is an assign- ment of an (internal) dihedral angle to each edge of each tetrahedron, such that opposite edges carry the same",
